// Zellij config -> %APPDATA%\Zellij\config\config.kdl
// Note the `config` level. Verified on 0.44.3 via `zellij setup --check`,
// which prints [CONFIG DIR] and [LAYOUT DIR] explicitly.

// CRITICAL. Zellij normally claims a pile of Ctrl shortcuts, which fight
// Claude Code for the same keys. Locked mode passes everything straight
// through to the running application. Ctrl+g unlocks if you want Zellij's
// own keybindings interactively.
//
// Nothing is lost by locking: the macro pad drives tab navigation over the
// CLI, so Zellij's keybindings are never needed in normal use.
default_mode "locked"

// Start with the Claude layout. Lets the Windows Terminal profile stay as the
// plain `zellij.exe attach --create claude`.
default_layout "claude"

// Historic issue, NOT reproduced on 0.44.3 (retested 2026-08-14): setting
// this to pwsh.exe was reported to break per-tab cwd.
//   https://github.com/zellij-org/zellij/issues/4938
//   https://github.com/zellij-org/zellij/issues/5052
// Tested on 0.44.3 with cmd.exe, powershell.exe and pwsh.exe: all launch, and
// per-tab cwd works in every case. Left here so the symptom is recognisable if
// it regresses - if tabs open in the wrong directory, comment this out first.
//
// With nothing set you get cmd.exe, not PowerShell. There is no $SHELL on
// Windows, so if you want PowerShell you have to say so.
//
// "pwsh.exe" resolves via the WindowsApps app-execution-alias when PowerShell 7
// is the Store build. That works. Prefer it over the full versioned path, which
// contains a version number and breaks on the next pwsh update.
default_shell "pwsh.exe"

// Frames waste rows and add noise when most tabs are a single pane.
pane_frames false

// Session serialisation: an exited session stays in `zellij list-sessions`
// and resurrects with its tabs, names and directories.
session_serialization true

// PASTE LATENCY. 0.45 added mouse hover effects and pane grouping and turned
// them on by default. On native Windows that costs roughly a SECOND PER
// CHARACTER on paste - measured here on 0.45.1 as ~20s for 19 characters, in a
// plain pwsh pane and in Claude Code alike, while the same paste into Windows
// Terminal outside Zellij is instant.
//
// Mouse tracking puts every mouse report on the same input path as the paste,
// and each report drives a render. This one line is the whole fix: bisected
// against `mouse_mode`, `mouse_hover_effects`, `mouse_hover_tips` and
// `mouse_scroll_resize`, each of which can stay at its default. So the wheel,
// click-to-focus and Ctrl+scroll resize all still work - what goes is hover
// decoration and pane grouping.
//
// Do NOT reach for `mouse_mode false` instead. It also fixes the paste, and it
// costs you scrolling.
advanced_mouse_actions false
